DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Title IV Pos
 tsecondaryInstitutions: Workforce Pell Program Applications Open for Secon
 d Review Cycle Through Nov. 13\nServices\nJobs & Training\nUnemployment In
 surance\nDisability Services\nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statisti
 cs\nWorkforce Development\nTitle IV PostsecondaryInstitutions: Workforce P
 ell Program Applications Open for Second Review Cycle Through Nov. 13\nOct
 ober 14\, 2026\nFor Immediate Release\nMedia Contact: Autumn Mahoney\, Com
 munications Specialist |\nmedia.dol@maine.gov\nAUGUSTA -The\nState Workfor
 ce Development Board\n(SWDB) is accepting applications from Title IV posts
 econdary institutionsseeking stateapproval to offer programs eligible for 
 federal Workforce Pell Grants. Applications for the second review cycle ar
 e due Friday\, Nov. 13\nMaine's Workforce Pell application provides an onl
 ine process for eligible postsecondary institutions to seek approval to of
 fer short-term workforce training programs that meet\nfederal Workforce Pe
 ll Grant requirements\n. Applications are accepted on a rolling basis and 
 reviewed quarterly by the SWDB.\nWorkforce Pell expands federal Pell Grant
  eligibility to approved short-term workforce training programs that prepa
 re students for high-skill\, high-wage and in-demand careers. States are r
 esponsible for reviewing and certifying eligible programs before they are 
 submitted to the U.S. Department of Education for final approval.\n"Workfo
 rce Pell opens the door to new education and career opportunities for more
  people across our state\,"said Vaughan Woodruff\, chair of the State Work
 force Development Board."The program's support for training that connects 
 people with skills needed for Maine's workforce presents a significant opp
 o\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363858
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363858
